[[Maintenance therapy in classical follicular lymphoma]]

!! Design

GADOLIN compared ''obinutuzumab–bendamustine followed by obinutuzumab maintenance'' with ''bendamustine alone'' in rituximab-refractory indolent lymphoma, predominantly FL. Patients without progression in the combination arm could receive maintenance for up to 2 years.

!! Results and interpretation

PFS = progression-free survival; OS = overall survival; HR = hazard ratio.

In the updated overall indolent-lymphoma population, median PFS was ''25.8 versus 14.1 months'' (HR 0.57), and OS also improved; benefits were consistent in the FL subgroup. These outcomes support the combined strategy in this relapsed/refractory context. They cannot be assigned to maintenance alone because induction also differed and the control arm did not receive obinutuzumab. The OS finding should not be extrapolated to frontline maintenance. [[GADOLIN updated analysis, Cheson et al., 2018|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29584548/]]

Evidence reviewed September 7, 2026.
